1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,760
It's so hot.

2
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,850
Do you want barley tea or iced coffee?

3
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,690
Huh? You're cooking already?

4
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,170
I wanna start now.

5
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,030
Let's take a break first.

6
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:25,900
I wanna simmer the curry for a long time.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,490
Fine. Okay, I got it.

8
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:28,860
But let's have some water first.

9
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,900
Here, sit down.

10
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,890
I'll get you a cold drink.

11
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:39,610
You got a TV.

12
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:41,030
Yeah.

13
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:43,360
I don't watch TV much.

14
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:45,410
But you seem to like it.

15
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:47,440
Huh, you could tell?

16
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,250
It's totally obvious.

17
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:51,240
I've been pretty obsessed lately.

18
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,470
I just keep watching TV.

19
00:00:56,970 --> 00:00:59,050
Can I turn it on?

20
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:00,500
Go ahead.

21
00:01:18,390 --> 00:01:19,740
Here, drink up.

22
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,270
Thanks.

23
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:35,330
By the way,
I'm going to my parents' place tomorrow.

24
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:37,110
Really? Staying overnight?

25
00:01:37,110 --> 00:01:39,320
Yeah, my brother's coming too,

26
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:43,010
so my mom's been nagging me to show up.

27
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,290
That's the least you can do.

28
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:48,180
Be nice to your parents when they're alive.

29
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,470
Well, I guess so.

30
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,659
Hey.

31
00:01:59,030 --> 00:02:00,860
Do you know this movie?

32
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:05,020
No, this is my first time seeing it.

33
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:06,590
What about you?

34
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:11,010
I feel like I vaguely remember it.

35
00:02:11,010 --> 00:02:13,060
Maybe my parents saw it.

36
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:18,140
What's it about?

37
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,910
I don't really know yet.

38
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,800
They're just arguing really fast
the whole time.

39
00:02:24,645 --> 00:02:26,725
Feels kind of high-class.

40
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,760
Yeah, I've seen this before.

41
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:37,630
Just a glimpse from behind my parents.

42
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,440
I remember this part.

43
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:49,710
[Hagiwara]
Oh, my! Kazuaki!

44
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,920
Have you gotten taller?

45
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,930
"Oh, my"?

46
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:57,320
You definitely got taller.

47
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,900
I didn't.

48
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,110
You definitely did.

49
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:03,150
I didn't.

50
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,190
Hey.

51
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:08,530
<i>Remember to hydrate frequently,
use the air con properly,</i>

52
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:11,840
<i>and take good care of your health.</i>

53
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:18,575
Is this simmered too?

54
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:22,380
Well, I mean...

55
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:26,090
Yeah, well, it's stew.

56
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:27,435
Why?

57
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:30,395
No reason. Just wondering.

58
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:34,220
Thanks for the food.

59
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,980
Do you both cook for yourselves?

60
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:43,540
A bit. I get home pretty early.

61
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:46,170
Yeah, on weekends and stuff.

62
00:04:46,170 --> 00:04:48,980
Try to cook as often as you can.

63
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:54,030
Before, I didn't worry
because Kaori was there, but...

64
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:56,760
Come on, I can cook for myself at least.

65
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:59,060
Really...

66
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:01,231
Breaking up after even living together...

67
00:05:01,231 --> 00:05:03,460
Let go of that already.

68
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,850
She was cute, thoughtful,
and a good girl, too.

69
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:07,930
Mom.

70
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:13,800
Well, it was a bit unfortunate
she was from a single-parent home, but...

71
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:18,330
Well, you'd want a girl
from a normal family, huh?

72
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:20,350
What?

73
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:23,960
What?

74
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:27,740
So if your parents are divorced,
you're not normal?

75
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:33,840
Well, losing a parent is tragic, but...

76
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,700
divorce is different, isn't it?

77
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,240
Seriously?

78
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,130
So it's okay if they died?

79
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:41,860
Don't pick a fight.

80
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:44,000
I'm just saying normal is best.

81
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,450
Saying "normal" in this day and age...

82
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,670
What even is normal?

83
00:05:49,670 --> 00:05:52,150
Don't talk like a child.

84
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:55,980
You can think that because
you're normal and have never had it hard.

85
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,320
Right?

86
00:05:58,870 --> 00:06:00,390
Let's stop.

87
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:11,520
You're the worst.

88
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,760
I'm leaving.

89
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,240
Wait a sec.

90
00:06:17,150 --> 00:06:19,170
Do whatever you want.

91
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,710
I don't need you to come home anyway.

92
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:23,657
- Mom.
- About that...

93
00:06:24,516 --> 00:06:26,840
You should've said that earlier.

94
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,740
Hey, Kazuaki!

95
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:27,420
[Newspaper Company, Rom-Com, Old Movie]

96
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:37,860
[A Classic Old Newspaper Company
Rom-Com Movie]

97
00:07:50,050 --> 00:07:51,730
Hagiwara?

98
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:54,790
I'm back.

99
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,580
Did you eat?

100
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,800
A little, at my parents' house.

101
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,770
You're not sleeping there?

102
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:11,330
I ended up coming back.

103
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:13,518
I got into a fight with my mom.

104
00:08:14,210 --> 00:08:17,030
A fight? Why?

105
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,900
It's nothing big.

106
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:28,170
Well, I was definitely in the right,
but I felt like leaving.

107
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:30,580
No, you can't do that.

108
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:34,910
But she was completely unreasonable.

109
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:37,660
Still, coming back was too much.

110
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,560
She must've prepared
all sorts of food and stuff.

111
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,760
But she told me to leave.

112
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:45,450
I'm sure she didn't mean it.

113
00:08:45,450 --> 00:08:49,130
You rarely see her,
so you should've just sucked it up.

114
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:53,470
You should go back. There's time.

115
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:54,790
What?

116
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:59,877
Ride the train back,
when I'm already halfway home?

117
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,830
I'd look like an idiot.

118
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:06,160
- Yeah, because...
- Because my parents are alive?

119
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:10,480
Right, of course.

120
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:15,790
What could I possibly do or say
in response to that?

121
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:26,010
I understand what you're saying,
and you're right.

122
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:27,630
But...

123
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:31,600
being right like that
leaves no room for my feelings.

124
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:44,650
Sorry, I'm going home for today.

125
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,610
I'm always the one walking out.

126
00:10:06,610 --> 00:10:08,180
Hagiwara!

127
00:10:11,161 --> 00:10:14,241
Sorry, I know you came a long way.

128
00:10:15,330 --> 00:10:18,400
No, you didn't do anything wrong, Nakarai.

129
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,536
But I made you feel...

130
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:23,036
Really, it's not your fault.

131
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:27,861
I said something awful to you too.

132
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:33,700
Sorry, I'm going home for today.

133
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,830
I want to cool my head a bit.

134
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:39,740
Hagiwara...

135
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:43,630
It's really okay.

136
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:22,717
[Big Bro]

137
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:41,720
Oh, Nakarai. What's up?

138
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:43,150
Where's Hagiwara?

139
00:11:43,150 --> 00:11:45,140
He's in a meeting.

140
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,650
Looks like a long one.

141
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:49,690
Is something wrong?

142
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:54,582
No, it's fine.

143
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,140
Good work.

144
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:13,540
Good work.

145
00:12:19,290 --> 00:12:20,920
That's good.

146
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,590
Did something happen?

147
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:30,690
Why?

148
00:12:30,690 --> 00:12:33,280
No reason.

149
00:12:36,010 --> 00:12:37,870
What's this about?

150
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:47,110
Professor Tsuwabuki passed away.

151
00:12:47,110 --> 00:12:49,810
Huh? The one from college?

152
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,070
Yeah.

153
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:55,260
They already had the funeral.

154
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:57,680
I see.

155
00:12:59,530 --> 00:13:04,150
He came with us
on the German club trip, remember?

156
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:08,600
He laughed and said he was just the wallet.

157
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:12,280
He did say that. While drinking beer.

158
00:13:15,118 --> 00:13:18,168
I liked Professor Tsuwabuki,

159
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:23,410
despite how he ended up
leaving the university.

160
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,650
Me too.

161
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:39,260
Apparently, Fujisawa went to
the professor's funeral.

162
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:41,890
I see.

163
00:13:45,130 --> 00:13:46,760
I mean, I...

164
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:51,920
I never really thought well of Fujisawa.

165
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:55,380
I mean, when your parents died,

166
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:58,470
and you stopped coming to college...

167
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:05,810
I tried to contact you,
but Fujisawa kind of gently refused.

168
00:14:05,810 --> 00:14:07,130
Yeah.

169
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:12,750
It felt like you got isolated
because of Fujisawa.

170
00:14:17,350 --> 00:14:21,500
But hey, we can drink together
again like this,

171
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,630
and you're smiling like before.

172
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:29,790
I think that time was necessary.

173
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:42,700
Lately, I think about my parents a lot.

174
00:14:43,810 --> 00:14:46,840
It used to be our last chat,

175
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:50,190
and other regrets like that, but...

176
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:56,220
Lately, they're fun moments
or happy memories.

177
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,130
That kind of thing.

178
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,340
I see.

179
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:09,380
A toast.

180
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:14,090
To Professor Tsuwabuki and your parents.

181
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,400
Cheers.

182
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:41,258
[Nakarai Family Grave]

183
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:28,190
Hello. I didn't know you were here.

184
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:29,930
I'll visit again.

185
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,910
Sorry I haven't visited.

186
00:17:38,141 --> 00:17:39,381
But...

187
00:17:41,450 --> 00:17:43,450
I'm okay now.

188
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:49,790
Next time, I'll bring someone
I want you to meet.

189
00:18:10,632 --> 00:18:12,102
Nakarai.

190
00:18:21,710 --> 00:18:24,170
You could've called me.

191
00:18:25,063 --> 00:18:28,323
I just felt like waiting.

192
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:33,850
Sorry about the other day.

193
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:35,730
I said something awful.

194
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:40,130
Did you apologize? To your mom?

195
00:18:40,130 --> 00:18:42,780
No, not yet.

196
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:45,670
But you apologize to me so easily.

197
00:18:47,790 --> 00:18:49,816
Because I don't want you to hate me.

198
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:52,620
You're spoiled.

199
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:03,880
I went to visit my parents' grave today.

200
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,510
I see.

201
00:19:10,110 --> 00:19:13,470
I suddenly decided to. Finally.

202
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:23,160
Are you hungry? I'll make something.

203
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,390
Okay.

204
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:33,090
By the way, thanks for the phone.

205
00:19:33,090 --> 00:19:36,830
I couldn't believe I left it at your place.

206
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,340
I talked to your brother.

207
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,460
What? Why?

208
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,630
Because it kept ringing.

209
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,590
What did you talk about?

210
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:56,970
<i>I'm sorry my little brother
caused you trouble.</i>

211
00:19:57,650 --> 00:20:02,850
So, Hagiwara said he fought with your mom,

212
00:20:02,850 --> 00:20:04,810
but is everything okay?

213
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:06,840
It's fine.

214
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:08,910
Just a misunderstanding.

215
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,550
Misunderstanding?

216
00:20:11,550 --> 00:20:13,641
<i>Yeah. My mom started kind of</i>

217
00:20:13,641 --> 00:20:16,120
<i>putting down his ex-girlfriend's
family background.</i>

218
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,870
<i>And then he suddenly got angry.</i>

219
00:20:22,310 --> 00:20:24,480
From a child's perspective,

220
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:27,300
you always want your parent to be proper.

221
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:29,599
Someone without any prejudice.

222
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:31,460
<i>Yes.</i>

223
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:36,000
But since we're adults now,

224
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,330
my mom kind of let her true feelings slip.

225
00:20:39,330 --> 00:20:42,310
Like wanting a normal person as a spouse.

226
00:20:42,310 --> 00:20:44,830
Well, what even is normal, though?

227
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:51,610
I don't think either of them is wrong.

228
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:56,298
Yeah... Well, I guess,

229
00:20:57,200 --> 00:21:01,260
<i>that just means everyone wants
what's best for other people.</i>

230
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:14,340
Nakarai?

231
00:21:16,370 --> 00:21:22,460
Like how your mom made the stew
you and your brother like.

232
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:25,350
And your names, Kazuaki and Kazuteru.

233
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:28,530
Right, "Kazu" means "one".

234
00:21:28,530 --> 00:21:30,510
She said it'd be sad

235
00:21:30,510 --> 00:21:35,212
if they numbered us in order,
like some kind of ranking.

236
00:21:35,212 --> 00:21:36,495
Yeah...

237
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:39,192
You have good parents.

238
00:21:42,177 --> 00:21:45,697
Yeah, they're good parents.

239
00:21:48,820 --> 00:21:53,340
My parents were... good parents too.

240
00:21:58,770 --> 00:21:59,970
Yeah.

241
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:10,230
Huh?

242
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:14,730
I found it online.

243
00:22:14,730 --> 00:22:16,670
Is it mine?

244
00:22:16,670 --> 00:22:19,370
Yeah, all yours, Nakarai.

245
00:22:24,890 --> 00:22:27,790
I'm talking about the DVD.

246
00:22:27,790 --> 00:22:31,320
Yep. All yours.

247
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,950
I'm talking about the DVD, not you, okay?

248
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:35,760
I know.

249
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,970
Then why are you laughing?

250
00:22:38,607 --> 00:22:41,536
Why are you blushing, Nakarai?

251
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:44,180
Because it's hot.

252
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:50,320
Ask more. "Is it mine?"

253
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:51,820
Over and over.

254
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,530
Is it mine?

255
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:32,570
Your birthday is coming up soon, right?

256
00:23:32,570 --> 00:23:34,630
Yes, I've kept it open.

257
00:23:34,630 --> 00:23:36,130
Because I was happy the other day.

258
00:23:36,130 --> 00:23:39,520
You casually asked me out,
like it was nothing.

259
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,700
Cheers.

260
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:42,990
Why don't we drink over there?

261
00:23:42,990 --> 00:23:46,180
You and Nakarai are close, huh?

262
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,000
Did you maybe see that earlier?

263
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,860
Whenever it was an important moment,

264
00:23:49,860 --> 00:23:51,090
it was always raining.

265
00:23:51,090 --> 00:23:54,110
Don't go after someone else's man
with such half-hearted feelings.

266
00:23:54,110 --> 00:23:57,510
The pretty amazing Nakarai
on the other side...

267
00:23:57,510 --> 00:24:00,210
is for my eyes only.
